<level1><h1>The Son from America</h1>
<p>Notice the simple nouns the author uses to describe the home.</p>
<blockquote><p>The hut consisted of one room, which contained all their belongings: the table, the shelf for meat, the two beds, and the clay oven.</p></blockquote>
<blockquote><p>To strive, to seek, to find, and not to yield.</p><byline>Alfred, Lord Tennyson</byline></blockquote>
<epigraph><p>The journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step.</p><byline>Lao Tzu</byline></epigraph>
